    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="0906" n="1740" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1740"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 637.119/467</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant to the War Trade Board Representative in
                        Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Farnsworth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-06T16:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 7, 7.07 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 110, July 2. I have the personal assurance of Cuban authorities that the
                    manner of dealing with Spanish vessels relative to bunkers will be carried out
                    strictly in accordance with your recommendation. Mr. Morgan handed you
                    translation of the President’s decree of June 26 relative to bunkering
                    vessels.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Farnsworth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
